Verification only asserts the *shape* of the change (`grep -c '\-mod=vendor'` = 0, `grep -q '\-mod=readonly'`). Nothing exercises a module-mode build with no `vendor/` present, so an incomplete `go.mod` that `-mod=readonly` rejects would still pass. This is the prompt's core deliverable ("a fresh clone with no `vendor/` builds"). Confirmed feasible: `go build -mod=readonly ./...` exits 0 here with no `vendor/`.

Add after `:129`:
```bash
