The three `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/...` paths exist on this host, but `dark-factory config` reports `claudeDir: ~/.claude-yolo`, and `/home/node/.claude-yolo/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/` does **not** exist. If the container mounts only `~/.claude-yolo`, all three context references are dead and the agent silently loses its guidance. Not provably broken (the `claude-yolo` image may still mount `~/.claude`), hence High not Critical. Confirm the actual mount and rewrite the prefix if needed.

